⚡🇯🇵 The Japanese Defense Ministry has notified major defense companies of cuts in weapons spending from the next fiscal year, beginning in April 2027.

The move sparked widespread discontent, the Kyodo news agency reported, citing sources. In some cases, the cuts will amount to 50% to 70% compared to the expected amounts. However, this will not affect already existing contracts.

